    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just the heat, though. i'm pretty sure i'm preheating properly. it's more like... i'll see a perfect, even sear happening, and then in a literal heartbeat, it's like a little burst of darkness just takes over a section of the meat. \n\nit feels so intentional, like there's some little force in there just grabbing a spot and sabotaging it. do you think there's a chemical way to explain that kind of sudden, localized \"attack\"? like, where one tiny part of the steak just decides to go rogue while the rest is fine?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
